{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>And the heart of Pharaoh grew strong.</b> Not on his own; but as YHWH had spoken through Moses before He joined Aaron with him, saying to him: וַאֲנִי יָדַעְתִּי כִּי לֹא יִתֵּן אֶתְכֶם מֶלֶךְ מִצְרַיִם לַהֲלֹךְ (Exodus 3:19) — that he will not let you go of his own will — וְלֹא בְיָד חֲזָקָה (Exodus 3:19) — and I will that he not do this out of fear of My strong hand, so that he be unable to endure it. And so He did in this case: for after he continued to sin willfully and himself hardened his heart against his own nature, yet was in doubt whether he could endure it, his heart was strengthened in the manner that YHWH had spoken through Moses, and he resolved in his heart not to let himself be struck again."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:25:02.037777143Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}